1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,708
PASSENGER: Driver! Why is the bus FLYING?!

2
00:00:03,058 --> 00:00:05,365
JONAH: Nobody panic!
Everything is under control!

3
00:00:06,665 --> 00:00:10,896
EXECUTOR: This is Jonah Okafor.
Yesterday, he fixed phones for a living.

4
00:00:11,246 --> 00:00:16,246
Today, he is holding a ten-tonne bus
in the air. With one hand.

5
00:00:16,596 --> 00:00:22,750
And in about four seconds, he is going to
make the biggest mistake of his life.

6
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:26,977
JONAH: Please don't sneeze. Please
don't sneeze. Please don't—

7
00:00:27,327 --> 00:00:29,181
Ah... ah... CHOO!

8
00:00:30,981 --> 00:00:35,562
EXECUTOR: What would you do... if
everything you touched lost its gravity?

9
00:00:35,912 --> 00:00:42,886
To understand how a phone repair boy ended up
here, we have to go back one day. To

10
00:00:42,886 --> 00:00:44,758
the night a star died.

11
00:00:46,158 --> 00:00:50,388
Lagos. Twenty million people. And one
very small phone repair stall.

12
00:00:51,588 --> 00:00:55,400
JONAH: Madam... how many times
did you drop this phone?

13
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:56,650
CUSTOMER: Once.

14
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,538
JONAH: From where? An aeroplane?

15
00:00:59,738 --> 00:01:04,354
EXECUTOR: Jonah Okafor. Seventeen. He can
fix anything with a wire in it.

16
00:01:04,704 --> 00:01:10,473
What he cannot fix is the feeling that his
real life is happening somewhere else.

17
00:01:11,273 --> 00:01:16,238
TUNDE: Oya, phone boy! Fix my screen. My
daddy will pay you... eventually.

18
00:01:16,588 --> 00:01:19,281
JONAH: Your daddy has owed me since March.

19
00:01:20,081 --> 00:01:23,927
MRS. BELLO: My husband's radio. It has
been silent since he passed.

20
00:01:24,277 --> 00:01:26,200
JONAH: Give me ten minutes, Ma.

21
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,769
EXECUTOR: He fixed it in nine. He would not
take her money. So Kemi paid instead.

22
00:01:33,119 --> 00:01:36,581
KEMI: It's my last toffee.
So it's worth a lot.

23
00:01:36,931 --> 00:01:40,392
JONAH: Then I'll save it for
a very important day.

24
00:01:40,742 --> 00:01:43,435
EXECUTOR: Nobody else saw
that. Remember it anyway.

25
00:01:44,235 --> 00:01:47,696
GRANDMA: Jonah! Bring this fridge
upstairs before I sell you!

26
00:01:48,046 --> 00:01:50,738
JONAH: Grandma, that fridge
weighs more than me!

27
00:01:51,088 --> 00:01:52,242
GRANDMA: Then eat more!

28
00:01:53,342 --> 00:01:59,980
EXECUTOR: That night, Jonah did what he always did.
He climbed to the roof, to look at places

29
00:01:59,980 --> 00:02:01,419
he would never go.

30
00:02:01,769 --> 00:02:02,669
JONAH: One day.

31
00:02:04,069 --> 00:02:09,035
EXECUTOR: Up there is Orion. And on his
shoulder... a red star. Betelgeuse.

32
00:02:10,235 --> 00:02:15,585
It is so big that if you put
it where our Sun is...

33
00:02:15,935 --> 00:02:19,012
it would swallow Mercury.
Venus. Earth. And Mars.

34
00:02:20,612 --> 00:02:25,577
That night, it died. Not with an
explosion. It just... switched off.

35
00:02:25,927 --> 00:02:28,585
JONAH: ...Did that star just turn off?

36
00:02:29,985 --> 00:02:33,831
EXECUTOR: But before it went dark,
it sent something to Earth.

37
00:02:34,181 --> 00:02:35,081
Twelve somethings.

38
00:02:36,681 --> 00:02:42,415
One of them landed in the hand of a
boy who was... fast asleep.

39
00:02:44,615 --> 00:02:47,658
JONAH: ...Why is the sky on the floor?

40
00:02:48,008 --> 00:02:50,700
EXECUTOR: The cat was not
enjoying this either.

41
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:52,800
JONAH: AAAAH!

42
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:56,612
GRANDMA: JONAH OKAFOR. Why is my
underwear on my head?!

43
00:02:57,812 --> 00:03:01,273
EXECUTOR: Jonah did what any
scientist would do. He experimented.

44
00:03:01,623 --> 00:03:05,400
JONAH: Open hand... it floats.
Close it... it falls.

45
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:10,012
And when I don't want it
to... nothing happens.

46
00:03:10,362 --> 00:03:13,823
GRANDMA: Why are you hugging
me? What did you break?

47
00:03:14,623 --> 00:03:16,162
EXECUTOR: Good morning, Jonah Okafor.

48
00:03:16,512 --> 00:03:22,588
That is the fourth flip-flop thrown at me
today. I believe it is how humans say

49
00:03:22,588 --> 00:03:23,050
hello.

50
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:30,646
I am the last machine of the Vey — the
people of the red star. Before their star

51
00:03:30,646 --> 00:03:36,508
went out, they gave away the one thing
they could not take with them.

52
00:03:36,858 --> 00:03:42,592
Their gifts. Twelve of them. Yours is
gravity. Or rather... the lack of it.

53
00:03:42,942 --> 00:03:44,865
JONAH: So I'm like an astronaut?

54
00:03:45,665 --> 00:03:51,481
EXECUTOR: Funny thing about astronauts. Up there,
gravity is still ninety percent as strong as

55
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:52,588
it is down here.

56
00:03:52,938 --> 00:03:54,862
JONAH: Then why do they float?

57
00:03:55,662 --> 00:04:01,550
EXECUTOR: Because they are falling. Fire a
cannonball fast enough, and the ground curves away

58
00:04:01,550 --> 00:04:02,969
as fast as it falls.

59
00:04:03,319 --> 00:04:08,674
It falls around the Earth. Forever. Astronauts
are not floating. They are falling...

60
00:04:08,674 --> 00:04:09,438
and missing.

61
00:04:09,788 --> 00:04:10,688
JONAH: And me?

62
00:04:11,038 --> 00:04:14,500
EXECUTOR: You, Jonah, do not
need to fall at all.

63
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,454
JONAH: Grandma! Watch this!

64
00:04:18,054 --> 00:04:22,955
EXECUTOR: Weightless is not the same as massless.
The fridge weighed nothing. It still had

65
00:04:22,955 --> 00:04:24,977
eighty kilograms of stubbornness.

66
00:04:25,327 --> 00:04:26,227
GRANDMA: JONAH!

67
00:04:27,327 --> 00:04:30,369
TUNDE: Phone boy! Is my screen ready, or—

68
00:04:30,719 --> 00:04:31,619
MY BIKE!

69
00:04:31,969 --> 00:04:36,585
EXECUTOR: Jonah had never been petty in
his life. He decided to start.

70
00:04:37,385 --> 00:04:40,812
JONAH: Okay. Okay! Now...
how do I go forward?

71
00:04:41,162 --> 00:04:46,931
EXECUTOR: Up there, you have nothing to push
against. You will have to push something else.

72
00:04:47,731 --> 00:04:52,312
Every push comes with a push back.
Throw something one way...

73
00:04:52,662 --> 00:04:55,319
JONAH: ...and I go the other way!

74
00:04:55,669 --> 00:04:57,592
IYA OSUN: My oranges! Who will pay?!

75
00:04:57,942 --> 00:05:00,250
JONAH: I'll pay you back, Iya! Tomorrow!

76
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:04,446
EXECUTOR: It is exactly how rockets
fly. They throw fire backwards.

77
00:05:05,246 --> 00:05:10,212
There was one small problem. Everything he
made weightless... started to rise.

78
00:05:10,562 --> 00:05:16,226
Air pushes up on everything. Normally, weight
wins. Take the weight away, and the

79
00:05:16,226 --> 00:05:18,254
air lifts it. Like a balloon.

80
00:05:18,604 --> 00:05:24,758
The goat would like it on record that
it did not agree to any of this.

81
00:05:25,558 --> 00:05:30,523
Three o'clock. Lagos traffic. One broken
bus. And behind it... an ambulance.

82
00:05:30,873 --> 00:05:32,412
JONAH: I can move that.

83
00:05:32,762 --> 00:05:34,300
EXECUTOR: Jonah. Remember the balloon.

84
00:05:34,650 --> 00:05:36,188
JONAH: What could go wrong?

85
00:05:36,988 --> 00:05:39,296
PASSENGER: Driver! Why is the bus FLYING?!

86
00:05:39,646 --> 00:05:42,338
JONAH: Okay, I've got it! I've got it!

87
00:05:42,688 --> 00:05:44,612
EXECUTOR: He did not have it.

88
00:05:45,412 --> 00:05:47,265
JONAH: Ah... ah... CHOO!

89
00:05:47,615 --> 00:05:53,191
EXECUTOR: And that brings us back to the mistake.
Ten tonnes, three metres up, falling... and

90
00:05:53,191 --> 00:05:55,273
the ambulance right underneath.

91
00:05:56,673 --> 00:06:02,408
His hand had closed. And then, for the
first time... he closed it slowly.

92
00:06:02,758 --> 00:06:04,962
JONAH: Slowly... slowly... slowly...

93
00:06:05,762 --> 00:06:11,915
EXECUTOR: That is the most important rule of
having a gift. Never let go all at once.

94
00:06:12,265 --> 00:06:15,692
PASSENGER: Young man... can
you do my house next?

95
00:06:16,492 --> 00:06:18,381
TUNDE: ...Okay. That was cool.

96
00:06:18,731 --> 00:06:24,828
EXECUTOR: By sunset, eleven million people had
watched it. One of them was the richest man on

97
00:06:24,828 --> 00:06:25,269
Earth.

98
00:06:26,069 --> 00:06:28,762
KADE: Jonah Okafor. Desmond
Kade. I build rockets.

99
00:06:29,112 --> 00:06:33,342
Do you know what the heaviest
part of a rocket is?

100
00:06:34,142 --> 00:06:38,758
The fuel. Nine-tenths of every rocket
is fuel, just to fight gravity.

101
00:06:39,108 --> 00:06:41,800
Now imagine a rocket that weighs nothing.

102
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:49,193
Float my rockets, and we go to Mars for the
price of a bus ticket. My jet leaves

103
00:06:49,193 --> 00:06:50,677
tonight, at eight.

104
00:06:51,027 --> 00:06:51,927
JONAH: Mars...?

105
00:06:52,277 --> 00:06:56,508
GRANDMA: And who will fix the
phones? Who will fix my fridge?

106
00:06:56,858 --> 00:06:58,012
JONAH: Grandma. It's MARS.

107
00:06:58,362 --> 00:07:02,942
GRANDMA: ...Then go. Before I cry
in front of a rich man.

108
00:07:03,742 --> 00:07:10,204
EXECUTOR: Before you go. You are not the only one.
Twelve gifts. Twelve people. Eleven of them

109
00:07:10,204 --> 00:07:11,435
do not know yet.

110
00:07:11,785 --> 00:07:12,938
JONAH: Does Kade know?

111
00:07:13,288 --> 00:07:14,442
EXECUTOR: He is counting.

112
00:07:15,242 --> 00:07:19,088
Seven-forty. Twenty minutes to his
flight. The rain came early.

113
00:07:20,688 --> 00:07:22,996
MRS. BELLO: KEMI! My
granddaughter is under there!

114
00:07:23,346 --> 00:07:24,850
JONAH: ...Stop the bike.

115
00:07:26,250 --> 00:07:30,096
EXECUTOR: He made the whole roof
weightless. Forty people crawled free.

116
00:07:31,496 --> 00:07:36,846
But Kemi was still on it. And it was
rising... into the lightning.

117
00:07:37,196 --> 00:07:38,096
KEMI: JONAH!

118
00:07:39,496 --> 00:07:42,888
JONAH: Push something... I
need to push something...

119
00:07:43,238 --> 00:07:46,700
EXECUTOR: His phone. His
ticket. His way out of Lagos.

120
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:49,038
He threw it away.

121
00:07:51,038 --> 00:07:52,577
KEMI: Jonah? Are we flying?

122
00:07:52,927 --> 00:07:56,004
JONAH: Just for a little
bit. Hold on tight.

123
00:07:56,804 --> 00:07:59,881
EXECUTOR: Slowly. Slowly.
Never let go all at once.

124
00:08:00,231 --> 00:08:01,131
MRS. BELLO: Kemi!

125
00:08:02,531 --> 00:08:03,685
KEMI: You kept it!

126
00:08:04,035 --> 00:08:07,881
JONAH: You said to save it for
a very important day.

127
00:08:08,231 --> 00:08:10,888
TUNDE: ...I will pay for your phone.

128
00:08:11,688 --> 00:08:13,227
KADE: You missed your flight.

129
00:08:13,577 --> 00:08:14,731
JONAH: I was busy.

130
00:08:15,081 --> 00:08:21,615
KADE: So I saw. There are eleven more of you
out there, Jonah. I wonder which of them

131
00:08:21,615 --> 00:08:22,773
won't be busy.

132
00:08:23,573 --> 00:08:25,112
GRANDMA: So. Mars is cancelled?

133
00:08:25,462 --> 00:08:26,615
JONAH: Mars can wait.

134
00:08:26,965 --> 00:08:28,504
GRANDMA: Good. The fridge cannot.

135
00:08:29,304 --> 00:08:32,765
EXECUTOR: Jonah Okafor did not
go to Mars that night.

136
00:08:33,115 --> 00:08:38,885
It turned out Lagos was not ready to
let him go. And neither was he.

137
00:08:40,885 --> 00:08:43,158
JONAH: Executor... why are there thirteen?

138
00:08:43,508 --> 00:08:45,046
EXECUTOR: Twelve gifts were sent.

139
00:08:45,896 --> 00:08:46,796
Thirteen arrived.

140
00:08:47,146 --> 00:08:49,804
That... is not supposed to happen.

141
00:08:51,404 --> 00:08:56,019
Next: a seventy-one-year-old grandmother in
Yorkshire who just jumped over a bus.

142
00:08:56,369 --> 00:08:57,908
MAGS: Well. That is new.

143
00:08:59,308 --> 00:09:03,119
EXECUTOR: And if you're wondering
whether it could be you...

144
00:09:04,069 --> 00:09:05,223
I'm still reading.
